+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries an API key: `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are
+kept in the data as `apiKeys` (see `docs/DATA.md`); each has a role:
+
+- `viewer`: may read (every `GET` route except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook`: as viewer, and may also cook recipes, record waste, log
+  temperatures and enter stock-take counts (the routes marked *cook* below).
+- `manager`: may do everything.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`
+(before anything else, even for routes that do not exist). A known key whose
+role may not use the route answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than `GET` from a known key, whether it succeeds or
+fails, writes one audit entry `{ id, at, key, method, path, status }`, where
+`key` is the key's name (never the key itself) and `path` has no query string.
+`GET /audit` lists them newest first.
+
+## Routes
+
+Who may call each route: *viewer* (any key), *cook* (cook or manager) or
+*manager*.
+
+- *viewer*: `GET /items`, `GET /items/:id`, `GET /batches`,
+  `GET /batches/:id`, `GET /orders/:id`, `GET /reports/stock-value`,
+  `GET /reports/waste?from=&to=`, `GET /alerts`, `GET /suppliers`,
+  `GET /suppliers/:id/prices?on=`, `GET /items/:id/best-price`,
+  `GET /dishes`, `GET /reports/margins`, `GET /recipes/:id/cost`,
+  `GET /forecast/use/:itemId`, `GET /forecast/reorder`, `GET /outbox`,
+  `GET /recipes/:id/allergens`, `GET /reports/allergens`,
+  `GET /reports/temperatures?day=`, `GET /export/ledger.csv`,
+  `GET /export/stock.csv`.
+- *cook*: `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures`, `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- *manager*: `POST /orders`, `POST /orders/:id/send`,
